  "method": "All absolute path coordinate pairs are mapped with hand-chosen landmark deltas. For limb points, locate source y between successive landmarks and interpolate delta with t*t*(3-2*t); clamp outside the limb range. Translate body/mane and skull as intact masses. Tail delta fades toward its tip. Region indices: tail 0-1, rear-far 2-3, front-far 4-5, body 6-9, rear-near 10-12, mane 13-15, front-near 16-19, head 20-30. Remove source toe-cut path 31 because its coordinates belong to old feet. Author a broad two-plane neck bridge between body/head masses after path 19; contact gets a modest separate lower jaw. Exact final SVG files are the durable authored sources, not a claim of rigged motion.",
  "limitations": "2D point fitting, not skeletal IK or a 3D rig. Paw support and negative space need visual review; no timing, transition interpolation or continuous velocity is established."
